From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UN1CA <unica@localhost>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Select Exynos2100 MIDAS LITE profile

The One UI 9 native loader reads ro.soc.model and falls back to missing V270
graphs on Exynos2100. Extend the existing LSI GPU/SNAPLITE profile, whose
tensor names and per-scale channels match the retained target LITE graphs.
Keep every other One UI 9 profile, including Pro/GenSR and the default.

This only repairs ordinary 2X/3X/4X model selection. The declared 1X graph
is not supplied; do not substitute a differently shaped graph or claim
that model presence establishes inference or full One UI 9.5 parity.
---
 midas_config.json | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/midas_config.json b/midas_config.json
--- a/midas_config.json
+++ b/midas_config.json
@@ -1522,12 +1522,12 @@
                 "SRIBMidas_aiUPSCALER_1X_LITE_V100_INT8.tflite",
                 "SRIBMidas_aiUPSCALER_2X_LITE_V100_INT8.tflite",
                 "SRIBMidas_aiUPSCALER_3X_LITE_V100_INT8.tflite",
                 "SRIBMidas_aiUPSCALER_4X_LITE_V100_INT8.tflite"
                 
               ],
               "models_list": [
-                "s5e9955"
+                "s5e9955", "Exynos 2100"
               ]
             }
           ],
           "residual_value": 0.7,
